WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.840
Enjoy your first day release.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.677
[spanish]

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:19.953
As I walked through the
doors, I couldn't believe it.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.722
It wasn't just some crazy dream.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.801
I might actually
get away with this.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:43.443
My stomach's churning over,
tying itself up in knots.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.461
I got on the bus.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:04.330
I'm praying that I'm never going
to see this place ever again.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.372
The bus starts moving.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:15.942
It felt amazing.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.110
It felt great.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.685
I'm feeling more and more
free and less and less

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.653
like a prisoner.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:36.629
But the closer we get to the
border, I'm getting so nervous.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:43.536
The last bit of the journey
is the most dangerous.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.207
The bus drives up
to the checkpoint.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.908
There's guardia everywhere.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:58.651
Not every car gets stopped,
so when we got pulled over,

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:04.324
my heart literally
dropped into my stomach.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.393
I stand out in Venezuela
with blue eyes.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.498
I can't have the
guardia seeing my eyes.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:14.434
If it's the guardia that's
worked in the prisons,

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.902
he's going to recognize me.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:19.005
[bleep] myself.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:23.009
[speaking spanish]

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.645
So I pretend to be asleep.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:29.282
I'm praying that they don't
ask to see my passport.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:32.385
[speaking spanish]

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.620
NARRATOR: They scan it.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.355
It's going to pop up
that I'm a prisoner.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.363
When the guard asked
the guy next to me,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.664
I'm thinking this is it.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:49.168
I'm [bleep]

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.803
[speaking spanish]

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.406
NARRATOR: And then he
asks me for my passport.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:03.383
Before I've had time to
think, the bus driver

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.286
says there's no point in
talking to the gringa.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.321
She can't speak a
word of Spanish.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.459
OK.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.862
NARRATOR: And the guardia
doesn't question it.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:19.132
I literally cannot believe
what has just happened.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:23.236
I feel like I've got
guardian angels around me.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.050
I've just escaped prison.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:41.187
I deserved my sentence.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.657
But I'm getting
closer to Nikita.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.661
It was the best
feeling in the world.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:04.077
I can't believe that was my
daughter in front of my eyes.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.979
She's five years older.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:09.048
And she looks so different.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.583
I said, you know
what my name is?

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.417
She said, no.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.086
And I said, my name is Natalie.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.722
And she said, are you my mummy?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.991
I said, yes, I am your mummy.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.727
And I always will be.

